Scratch that idea, leave the call where it is. I forgot that `CalculateVolumeConstraintVolumes` doesn't look at the rest length but at the vertices. What you want to do instead is to add a loop after this for loop that does:

```C++
float multiplier_pow_3 = multiplier * multiplier * multiplier;
for (JPH::SoftBodySharedSettings::Volume &v : settings->mVolumeConstraints) {
   v.mSixRestVolume *= multiplier_pow_3;
}
```

Rationale: The volume is calculated using `(edge1 cross edge2) dot edge3`, we're scaling all edges with `multiplier` so the volume becomes `((multiplier * edge1) cross (multiplier * edge2)) dot (multiplier * edge3)` = `multiplier_pow_3 * ((edge1 cross edge2) dot edge3)`

