body:
`CreateConstraints` takes the faces of the soft body and creates edge, bend and LRA constraints for those faces. In the `_create_shared_settings_volume` function, you have already created edge constraints, so the result is that some of the edges will be created 2x. So for the 'volume' version you should not call `CreateConstraints`.

The compliance can be set on `Edge` and `Volume`, so:

```
v.mCompliance = compliance;
settings->mVolumeConstraints.push_back(v);
```

and 

```
settings->mEdgeConstraints.emplace_back(JPH::SoftBodySharedSettings::Edge((JPH::uint32)e.x, (JPH::uint32)e.y, compliance));
```

